  "findings_by_claim": {
    "C1": {
      "severity": "PASS",
      "supports": "United Airlines Holdings (CIK 0000100517) own filings repeatedly disclose Eve Holding / Eve Air Mobility: 7 hits on 'Eve Holding' and 4 hits on 'Eve Air Mobility' \u2014 across multiple 10-Qs (Q1 2023 through Q1 2024), 10-Ks (FY2022 and FY2023), the 2023 DEF 14A, and an October 2022 8-K (which is consistent with the September 2022 subscription closing).",
      "M_check": "edgar_fts.query_fulltext(cik=0000100517, term='Eve Holding') and (term='Eve Air Mobility')",
      "M_value": "Eve Holding hits=7; Eve Air Mobility hits=4. Earliest 8-K=2022-10-18 (matches Sept 2022 transaction). Recurring 10-Q/10-K disclosure through 2024-04-17.",
      "interpretation": "United independently and continuously discloses Eve in its own SEC filings \u2014 strong corroboration of the relationship and investment. Recurring presence across periodic reports indicates meaningful, ongoing related-party / strategic investment disclosure consistent with the $15M cash + $0.01 warrants structure described."
    },
    "C2": {
      "severity": "PASS",
      "supports": "External brand-validation hits show 41 mentions of 'Eve Air Mobility' and 170 mentions of 'Eve Holding' across all SEC filers. Most hits are Eve's own filings, but UAL, Mercury Systems, Garmin, and a SPAC (Direct Selling Acquisition) appear as independent filers referencing Eve. The disclosure itself flags non-binding nature, so the claim is calibrated to LOI-based industry-standard backlog reporting.",
      "M_check": "edgar_fts.query_fulltext term=Eve Air Mobility and term=Eve Holding cik=null",
      "M_value": "Eve Air Mobility total_hits=41; Eve Holding total_hits=170. Several non-Eve filers referencing the brand.",
      "interpretation": "Recipe is named_counterparty_order, but Eve explicitly characterizes the pipeline as non-binding LOIs from 29 customers \u2014 this is a well-disclosed soft-backlog claim. With external SEC footprint >40 hits and a PUBLICLY listed strategic customer (UAL) verifiable in C1, the order-pipeline narrative is supported by the kind of footprint a real industry participant would have. Per heuristic 7 (1-3 mentions = PASS/MODERATE), a count this high is clear PASS. We do not attempt per-customer LOI verification because the disclosure itself acknowledges they are non-binding."
    },
    "C3": {
      "severity": "PASS",
      "supports": "EPA FRS returns 0 facilities for 'Eve' in Melbourne FL \u2014 but per calibration heuristic 1 (offices/R&D/aviation test EXPECTED absent from EPA FRS) AND the EXPLICIT note that Eve uses Embraer's facilities royalty-free under the MSA/SSA, the Eve-name absence is non-signal. Querying the parent name returns 5 EPA-registered Embraer aerospace facilities in Melbourne FL \u2014 including 'EMBRAER AREA 1', 'EMBRAER ENGINEERING & TECHNOLOGY CENTER INC' (1400 General Aviation Dr), and 'EMBRAER EXECUTIVE AIRCRAFT' (3 sites on General Aviation Dr).",
      "M_check": "epa_frs.query_facilities (Eve, FL, Melbourne) and (Embraer, FL, Melbourne)",
      "M_value": "Eve in Melbourne FL: n=0. Embraer in Melbourne FL: n=5 (Area 1, Engineering & Technology Center, 3x Executive Aircraft sites all on General Aviation Dr).",
      "interpretation": "Real, geo-confirmed aerospace complex on General Aviation Drive in Melbourne FL adjacent to Melbourne Orlando International. The 'Engineering & Technology Center' name is exactly the kind of facility that would host Eve's Florida operations under the MSA shared-services structure. Geo-coordinates cluster at lat 28.10-28.11, lon -80.64. Claim PASSES via parent-name lookup as anticipated by calibration."
    },
    "C4": {
      "severity": "UNVERIFIABLE",
      "supports": "EDGAR full-text search of Embraer ADR (CIK 0001355856) returns 0 hits for 'Eve Holding', 0 for 'EVE UAM', 0 for 'urban air mobility', 0 for 'eVTOL' \u2014 and crucially 0 for the term 'Embraer' itself. This indicates Embraer's filings (6-K furnishings; foreign-private-issuer 20-F) are not indexed in the EDGAR FTS pipeline used here, so absence is structural, not a signal. Per calibration heuristic 2 (foreign-issuer ADR: 0-2 mentions = NORMAL).",
      "M_check": "edgar_fts.query_fulltext cik=0001355856 (Embraer ADR) for multiple Eve-related terms",
      "M_value": "0 hits across 4 search terms (Eve Holding, EVE UAM, urban air mobility, eVTOL); also 0 hits for 'Embraer' itself, confirming structural index gap.",
      "interpretation": "EDGAR FTS cannot verify or contradict this claim because Embraer's 6-K/20-F filings do not appear in the index. Per the explicit calibration for foreign issuers, this is NOT a red flag. Indirect support exists: EPA FRS confirms Embraer's Melbourne FL aerospace operations (C3), and USPTO confirms Embraer's deep aviation IP estate (162 granted US patents \u2014 see C5). The MSA/SSA narrative is consistent with what a real Embraer subsidiary would receive. Marking UNVERIFIABLE rather than RED_FLAG because the data source is structurally unable to test FPI counterparties."
